2186045417] [17592186069896 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7b713819-4a19-57c4-9270-3799e69d5f61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069896 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069897 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069897 #edb/ref 1061 6164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069897 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fa4f9a55-e5d6-50e4-a705-d8fcd6cacddb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069897 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069949 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we want to plot the curve $y=x^2.$ We start by making a table of values.\n\n| **$x$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=x^2$ | $9$ | $4$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ |\n\nWe can now plot the graph using the $(x,y)$ values in our table.\n\n![](images/57/576148f61e683e58c508b212221c103d9ef9914f549afabfec92a04ec778a268.png)\n\nThis curve's shape is known as a **parabola**, and the **minimum point** at $(0,0)$ is known as the **vertex** of the parabola." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069949 #edb/ref 1065 1633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069949 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "98e8af90-38c4-57f6-a494-cc5214d10c9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069949 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069952 #edb/ref 1064 "Horizontal and vertical translations can be combined. It does not matter which we do first.\n\nIn general, the graph of $y=(x-h)^2+k$ is a translation of the standard parabola $y=x^2$ by\n\n- $h$ units right, and\n\n- $k$ units up.\n\nThe vertex of $y=(x-h)^2+k$ is located at $(h,k).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069952 #edb/ref 1065 1853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069952 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b17f43fa-0d9e-5d24-b900-72a6dececdad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069952 #edb/ref 1067 "Combinations of Horizontal and Vertical Translations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069953 #edb/ref 1064 "The graph of  ![](images/78/7816c015ff36e92e579c157d0d1e074270678c48b06f0c2d37d920311224d5e5.svg) looks like the standard parabola ![](images/2e/2eb046be7e52e5a72d29a1333f9cf483411f0a8d6d897fe53014cc1952c6f759.svg), but shifted ![](images/6c/6cb44f25e489afb06ec62d2e95c4d235ece77eb36e2327b856264d2fb8b22c21.svg) units to the *right* along the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-axis. \n\n![](images/a4/a48db73aadd4192f244676c3cb54c6849ca284acf1adbf29d6245baa5a07afcb.png)\n\nSimilarly, the graph of ![](images/ce/ce16aa1f1cc35aaeae8aba5c19c0ebf1e9ea43e9624f0c6c18b42f7bfa21c304.svg) looks like the standard ![](images/2e/2eb046be7e52e5a72d29a1333f9cf483411f0a8d6d897fe53014cc1952c6f759.svg) parabola after it's been shifted ![](images/f5/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) units to the *left*:\n\n![](images/9c/9c33ae042e23cee23f96a35f31afbb3f80fb1dfece702b26c2a1aded17885861.png)\n\nIn general, the graph of ![](images/4b/4b00aba256457d4efcd4f517482795d922665890adf0c2f0c0991527b5c1edfb.svg) looks like the standard parabola ![](images/2e/2eb046be7e52e5a72d29a1333f9cf483411f0a8d6d897fe53014cc1952c6f759.svg) but translated ![](images/99/994427fe929fdf538d7c1be792e6fa4b85697f0921161bf5ddf0e639864c9f27.svg) units right. The vertex of ![](images/4b/4b00aba256457d4efcd4f517482795d922665890adf0c2f0c0991527b5c1edfb.svg) is located at ![](images/ef/efb3fb22e5e729a56d75a55b8e4b43e7ebf0cb77a3798550afdf9e05ac3a1525.svg)\n\n**Watch Out!** It's easy to confuse the translations.\n\n- For ![](images/78/7816c015ff36e92e579c157d0d1e074270678c48b06f0c2d37d920311224d5e5.svg), we subtract ![](images/6c/6cb44f25e489afb06ec62d2e95c4d235ece77eb36e2327b856264d2fb8b22c21.svg) from ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) inside the parentheses, and the parabola moves to the right, *not* to the left (even though it seems like it should be the other way around).\n\n- Likewise, for ![](images/ce/ce16aa1f1cc35aaeae8aba5c19c0ebf1e9ea43e9624f0c6c18b42f7bfa21c304.svg), we add ![](images/f5/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) to ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) inside the parentheses, and the parabola moves to the left, *not* to the right." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069953 #edb/ref 1065 1854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069953 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5e424d1b-91e1-5860-b0c9-5ca519476af7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069953 #edb/ref 1067 "Horizontal Translations of a Parabola" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069980 #edb/ref 1064 "Adding a value to ![](images/2e/2eb046be7e52e5a72d29a1333f9cf483411f0a8d6d897fe53014cc1952c6f759.svg) will **translate** (shift) the parabola up or down the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis. For instance, adding ![](images/f5/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) to ![](images/2e/2eb046be7e52e5a72d29a1333f9cf483411f0a8d6d897fe53014cc1952c6f759.svg) will move each point on the parabola ![](images/f5/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) units up.\n\n![](images/2a/2a233fc5fe21dd3ffd460ab3fa343ac3c4587bca17fd958343309bc723a2cda5.png)\n\nOn the other hand, subtracting ![](images/6c/6cb44f25e489afb06ec62d2e95c4d235ece77eb36e2327b856264d2fb8b22c21.svg) will move each point of the parabola ![](images/6c/6cb44f25e489afb06ec62d2e95c4d235ece77eb36e2327b856264d2fb8b22c21.svg) units down.\n\n![](images/5b/5bcc36e857503b3faf90d1cbb58750150dc7849a0f2a0b3c58b77319ffff1224.png)\n\nIn general, the graph of ![](images/00/00abc9adb93347077819fc66fecc1e7eef09e68fc6f8e94a76e27c8eb70b13a0.svg) looks like the standard parabola ![](images/2e/2eb046be7e52e5a72d29a1333f9cf483411f0a8d6d897fe53014cc1952c6f759.svg) but translated ![](images/8d/8dc6f7e80ecaac9fa07890ce1881dd51de319597ae8b1dce821aa03c1f3eff06.svg) units up. The vertex of ![](images/00/00abc9adb93347077819fc66fecc1e7eef09e68fc6f8e94a76e27c8eb70b13a0.svg) is located at ![](images/e8/e8c4c8598a8228afb25cbf13c034e2fe234393f9b9c0dfde8be1726b4fc79a8e.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069980 #edb/ref 1065 4230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069980 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "82fdbf6d-9723-58e6-ba17-37a663d4fe1c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069980 #edb/ref 1067 "Vertical Translations of a Parabola" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528312 #edb/ref 1080 "images/a5/a5313544206d95a45b695bfeb6bc05ced0c113fe0e64760de3c8b9f618aa3749.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528312 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528312 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04cf61b8-04db-5f45-abb5-90fdc5ad1da5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528382 #edb/ref 1080 "(0,3)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528382 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528382 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1e90deef-05f5-54f7-b6b5-a60fc604504b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528385 #edb/ref 1080 "(5,5)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528385 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528385 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "200a5054-afad-5419-87fd-fdd2e2f96547" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528402 #edb/ref 1080 "images/4e/4e43c68bd7ab2da6fb0be21ecc69ab29e111c442219caaae70b819e9df3488be.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528402 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528402 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "29128bb6-698e-5f80-b2d5-1fcc609cce2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528454 #edb/ref 1080 "(5,2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528454 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528454 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3c31527b-b7bb-56c0-ae70-dc74a4214f25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528464 #edb/ref 1080 "y=8{x}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528464 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528464 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "406deb7b-69c7-5514-9